---
description: Automatic token bounds on every prompt.
alwaysApply: true
---

Default to Cursory tools before native dumps:
- search → `cursory_smart_search`
- symbol/range/file reads → `cursory_smart_read`
- tests/builds/logs/diffs → `cursory_smart_run`
- missing lines → `cursory_get_raw` (not `force_full`)

Native Read/Grep/Shell may already be capped; treat truncation as intentional.
Skip the efficient-context skill. Do not call Cursory just to announce or plan.
Keep exact source — never summarize to save tokens.
